\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The cost of causality. Under power-law impact the adapted value is a fixed fraction of the clairvoyant value, $v/v_{\rm  ant}=\sin (\pi \beta /2)$ of~\eqref  {eq:sinlaw}, independent of the signal speed: adaptedness is nearly free for short-memory impact ($\beta \to 1$) and forfeits almost all the value for near-permanent impact ($\beta \to 0$), keeping between a third and four-fifths of the clairvoyant value over the empirical range (shaded).}}{9}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
